                        <surname>Macmillan</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>printer</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Macmillan was one of Godwin's printers. The fourth edition of Godwin's book <title>The Pantheon: or Ancient History of The Gods
    of Greece and Rome</title> (1814) was printed by B. Macmillan of Bow Street, Covent Garden. However, there are no printers called Macmillan on <title>The 
    British Book Trade Index</title> that match the dates and hence no further information available.</p>
                        <p>One instance of Macmillan occurs in 1800 which precedes the majority of the contacts by five years; thus, it may not be the same person.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> Marshall, <title>William Godwin</title></bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Locke, <title>A Fantasy of Reason</title></bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>The British Book Trade Index</title>
                    </bibl>
